node_modules/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DERIVED — never committed. Rebuilt by `npm run pipeline`, deterministically.
#
# The rule: commit what a human wrote and what cannot be re-fetched; do not
# commit what the pipeline derives.
#
#   pipeline/raw/      committed — fetched from upstream, and upstream has
#                      already lost data once (2022's matches array is gone)
#   pipeline/lookups/  committed — hand-curated
#   pipeline/overlays/ committed — hand-written video dataset
#   data/              IGNORED   — derived from the three above
#   pipeline/normalized/ IGNORED — derived from raw
#
# Committing the derived trees put 1,506 files and 13 MB into git to describe
# data the build inlines into HTML anyway. The same mistake was made three times
# in this project (per-match raw details, per-match published data, team-season
# pages) before it was written down here as a rule.
#
# The determinism guarantee is what makes this safe: the same inputs produce
# byte-identical output, so nothing is lost that cannot be regenerated exactly.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/
pipeline/normalized/
dist/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
